RECONCILIATIONS (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
R1 OUTPUT PATH. The generated prompt names the output
   `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/ApiLogsPage.swift`. That directory is NOT a
   source root in `apps/apple/project.yml` (the iOS/macOS app targets compile
   `Sources/**` + `TeslaSync/{feature-views,dashboard-widgets,misc-surfaces,
   shared-surfaces,widget-primitives}` + `Localization` + the generated tokens). A
   file under `TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**` would never be compiled. EVERY sibling
   admin page (AuditLog, ApiPlayground, DiskForecast, FeatureFlags,
   FleetTelemetryCoverage, LiveSignalInspector, SchemaDrift, TeslaOrders) lives in
   `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/`. The page is implemented there to match the
   built, shipping convention (identical to the AuditLog precedent's recorded path
   reconciliation). Tests go in `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/` (the
   `TeslaSyncTests` / `TeslaSync-macOSTests` bundles).

R2 STRING KEYS. Web `apiLogs.*` keys are mirrored into the platform catalog under the
   `translation.` namespace (the i18next default ns), exactly like the TeslaOrders
   sibling (`orders.title` → `translation.orders.title`). All 30 required strings
   already exist in `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` as
   `translation.apiLogs.*` (29) + `translation.error.loadFailed` (1) — verified
   present; ZERO new string keys were needed for the 43 parity items. Only the
   navigation title `route.apiLogs` (+ `spotlight.route.apiLogs.description`) was
   added for the new `AppRoute` case.

R3 DATA SOURCES. The manifest auto-detector recorded "no API data sources"; the web
   page in fact reads two feeds (`getAPICallLogStats` + `getAPICallLogs`) via
   `@/api/devtools` (which the detector's `@/api/hooks/use*` heuristic misses). The
   page is implemented faithfully with both feeds bound through an `@Observable`
   model + injectable `ApiLogsDataSource` seam (production binds the KMP dev-tools
   endpoints; ADR-004 — no networking in the view), driving all four declared data
   states. This is additive faithfulness, never a shortcut.

R4 EXPORT + DATE RANGE. Web `handleExport` (browser blob download) → HIG-native
   `ShareLink(item:)` over the model's `exportJSON` (snake_case rows, disabled when
   empty). Web header `<RangePicker>` (a `PageContainer` action) → HIG-native
   toggle-gated start/end `DatePicker`s inside the filter panel (web
   `translation.apiLogs.startDate` / `endDate` labels). Both are real, working
   controls — no stubs.

