================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI ApiLogsPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
`@Observable` `ApiLogsPageModel` (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing the list
state (loading/empty/error/success), the independent stats feed, the filter row, the date
range, pagination, the row-expansion set, and the export JSON, over an injectable
`ApiLogsDataSource` seam whose value types mirror the web `APICallLog` / `APICallLogStats`
1:1 (production binds the KMP dev-tools endpoints). The page reproduces the web chrome
(title/subtitle), the "Failed to load data" banner, the four stat cards, the tappable
"By Service" chips, the filter panel (Service + serviceCount caption, Method, Status,
endpoint search, toggle-gated date range, Clear), and the entries panel — the "Showing …"/
"No logs" header with an Export-JSON ShareLink, the four list states, the adaptive
paginated rows (macOS/iPad row, iPhone stacked card), and the expandable detail (request
URL, error, and request/response JSON bodies) — using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components
(no hand-rolled glass). Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings via the
web key names (the translation.apiLogs.* mirror); number/latency/UTC-date/JSON formatting
and the {{token}} catalog interpolations are ported and unit-tested. Verified on BOTH idioms
by isolated Swift-6 strict-concurrency type-checks (macOS 0 / iOS 0, exercising the compact
branches) and an executed model harness (all assertions passed). The full xcodebuild scheme
is BLOCKED only by the absent KMP Frameworks/Shared.xcframework (out of scope, environment),
with ZERO diagnostics in any ApiLogs* file.

